Sorry to bore people here (do people actually read YAAP's??), but you
know the exhiliration that drives you when you finally ascend! :-) I
finally managed ascended genocide-less, and as it turns out, polyless.
This is also my first ascension on a public server.

I was almost wishless except for a stupid incident at the Castle (see
below), and the Planes turned out to be a lot tougher than I expected
this time round and I had to burn 4 more wishes. (Either that, or I
was inadequately prepared... see below).

Anyway, first of all, is there a way to get the ascension logs from
NAO? I didn't bother to copy-n-paste the ascend logs 'cos I thought I
should be able to access it readily, but when I logged in again, I
couldn't figure out how, so the following is purely from memory.


Durak started out as yet another botched protection racket attempt.
There were a couple of close shaves so he thought better and leveled
up to about Exp:3 or so before attempting to reach Minetown (grotto
version). Did some, uh, trading, at Minetown with the pet and a few
rare stones (ID'd by the trusty touchstone), and dug through many a
vault to get to about AC:0 by the time he was around Exp:8.

Basically, he was the continuation of my playing style of levelling up
as minimally as possible, so no wraith eating, period. At around
Dlvl:6, he found a bones pile of some poor mage, and inherited his
cursed magic marker and cloak of MR. Found some altars progressively
deeper in the dungeon, and spent a lot of time collecting and sorting
through equipment, found a magic whistle, acquired two pet dogs and
swindled many a shop with them (not much of a lawful there!). It was
amazing how quickly two dogs and a magic whistle creates empty shops.
:-P From the loot, Durak figured out most potions, and scrolls, etc.,
and found Fort Ludios at around Dlvl:14, and, with the "oRefl from
Sokoban at Dlvl:10 and his trusty tinning kit, he pretty soon acquired
most of his intrinsics. After that he went back to Minetown and maxed
out his AC, and reached Minebottom.

At this time, he was still Exp:12 at most, so he passed by the Quest
and when down all the way to Medusa, but didn't have a way to cross.
But by now, he finally reached Exp:14, and so went to the quest. By
this time, he had AC:-12 + MR + Refl, so the Minion of Huhetotl was a
joke. Then he found another altar down at Dlvl:18 or so, and moved his
camp there. Got two artifacts from saccing, but found them rather
useless (long swords for Arc just doesn't cut it). Then, during a trip
to Minetown, he accidentally attacked a watchman (hate the fact that
'y' is a movement key and a confirmation key for wanting to
attack---all it takes is for you to hit 'y' once too often). This
provoked the entire Minetown guard to come after him, and then he got
this bright idea that perhaps, if he dropped the /oDeath in front of
the watch captain, the captain might be tempted to use it. And he did:
and BOING! the death ray reflected back at the captain and he was
history, and Durak gets away with not killing a peaceful---at least,
not directly. :-P  Then he notices that the captain had a silver
saber, and decided to adopt this weapon, bringing it back to base camp
at Dlvl:18 and enchanting it to +6.

Then he went down to Medusa, dug through to the maze below
(surprisingly, the level below Medusa wasn't a maze, but the level
after that was... odd), and found a purple worm crawling around. He
took pity on it, and using a ?oTaming, brought the critter home and
christened it Obzhora. Well, he soon discovered what a voracious
appetite this thing had when he brought it down to the Castle and set
it loose. Unfortunately, during a botched drawbridge incident, a nymph
stole the +6 saber from him, leaving him only with a +0 pick-axe as a
weapon. In an attempt to get it back, he tried to use the whip to
snatch it but ended up killing the nymph over water. Oops! So a
hilarious aftermath ensued where he tried to push a boulder over and
dig through, only to find that water gushed in from the side; so he
burned up a wish for an amulet of magical breathing---but, living up
to his name, proceeded to forget about it and used up a ?oEarth in
another attempt to retrieve the weapon, and the square the nymph fell
into needed FOUR boulders before it filled up (the rest were used to
dam the moat). But digging through, the weapon wasn't found... so he
gave up and started using another saber found on a captain. Funnily
enough, later on when he came back to strip the slain, out of nowhere
he finds a +6 saber lying just a few squares from where the nymph was
killed, on dry land. How that happened, he had no idea, but he was
sure happy about it.

Meanwhile, he finally figured out that Obzhora could live up to its
name better if he zapped a ?oSpeed at it... and suddenly, burrrps
could be heard resounding from every corner of the dungeon...
including one incident when Durak decided to convert an altar in a
non-coaligned temple: before he could even provoke the priest,
BURRRRP!! and the priest was nowhere to be found.

So he brought his little pet down to the castle, where it feasted on
all sorts of delicacies, and down to the Valley, where it feasted on 3
graveyards of wraiths, reaching Exp:30 with 245 maxhp. So Durak was
starting to get cocky with his little purple pet, when suddenly a
chameleon appeared, disguised as some innocuous monster. BURRRRP! ...
and Obzhora turned into a feeble jackal. D'OH!

With wounded pride, Durak retreated to base camp at Dlvl:18, and
starting doing some alchemy and refining his equipment. Soon, he got
himself to AC:-30 or so, but hoped to finish the game without any
further wishes, so he kept his +3 leather gloves and made his own
dragonmail from scales he found somewhere. Then he went down the
Gehennom, and got so sick and tired of the endless mazes, that he
wielded his pick-axe, turned on autodig, and went berzerk... and soon,
60% of Gehennom had turned into Big Rooms. From this, he collected a
huge amount of loot, which he hauled back just before he reached
Dlvl:42, which was about a level or two past the Wizard Tower. (On the
way up he decided to have a little chat with Vlad, who told him in no
uncertain terms, "I vant to suck your blood!", and so told Vlad
exactly what he thought of his bad German accent.)

From this huge loot, he set up a chem lab at Dlvl:18 and managed to
get to HP:345/345 (after a few explosions), and made good use of the
poor old wizard's magic marker to get down to AC:-45. Then he packed
away his gems in a spare BoH, and stuffed it away next to the < at
Dlvl:1, bought 7 candles at an exorbitant cost from Itzchak's (at this
point he had no more use for money so he didn't care), and prepared
for the ascension run.

Turns out that his preparation was inadequate, as he had spent the
charges on his /oDeath way too freely. He got to Rodney's, and bounced
a death ray between two walls until Rodney relinquished the book, and
then rushed down to the Sanctum. The Sanctum was no problem with a
=oConflict, and another death ray bounced between the walls of the
Inner Sanctum, and the Amulet was his. So he pulled out a c!oGL and
left the slobbering masses to themselves. The mysterious force didn't
act for the first 6 levels or so, and then it started giving lots of
trouble. But, thanks to Durak's renovation of Gehennom into Big Rooms
(albeit incomplete), this didn't set him back too much. He used up the
rest of the c!oGL to get out of Gehennom, and then levitated through
the Castle and Medusa, and then was doing the home run, when trouble
struck. Well, that is to say, Double Trouble. Rodney appeared again,
and Durak gave him the /oDeath... but missed. THRICE. And then he
realized that the /oDeath had no more charges... and neither had the
other /oDeath in the bag. So Rodney, realizing his opportunity,
xeroxed himself and double-troubled Durak, summoning a master lich to
add to the annoyance.

With difficulty, Durak beat them back to the < and got them scampering
upstairs (fortunately, he still had the Amulet). He sat around to heal
up and kill off the rest of the critters, and then realized that he
had a magic marker and some blank scrolls with him, so he wrote a
?oCharging, recharged the /oDeath, went upstairs, and dispatched the
Rodney twins. The master lich got lucky, in that Durak came to his
senses that /oDeath charges need to be saved for emergencies, so when
Durak swindled him from his advantageous position on the <, the master
lich thought better and disappeared down a hole with a /oDigging.

After that, Durak made it to Dlvl:1 without further complications. He
grabbed his gems bag and ran upstairs, and had the idiocy to throw a
lighted potion of oil at Rodney. Maybe it was to avenge the double
trouble incident, and it was fun to watch Rodney's spellbooks burn,
but I think that was missing the point (after all, the +oDig was
really for Durak not for Rodney!), and it gave Rodney the chance to
summon an incredible number of monsters given the tiny space available
on that little bubble in the Plane of Earth. Fortunately, the /oDeath
dispatched Rodney once for all, and soon, Durak was digging his way to
the portal, found by c?oGD.

The Plane of Air was a disaster. Durak used up all his /oTeleport,
/oOpening, and /oDeath charges, and was less than half HP and still
only halfway to the portal. So he decided to take a more circuitous
route to the portal, stopping by to visit a few vortices on the way,
in which he nursed his wounds (and he had the audacity to not bring
any !oHealing's of any kind with him), and burned up a wish for a
/oDeath---he didn't get it. Then burned up another wish for a magic
marker to write ?oCharging's, and managed to make it to the portal
before the AE's finished him off.

Plane of Fire was easy: get inside a fire vortex and gaze at the Orb
of Detection, then use '/' to find the portal. On the way, he had the
idiocy to bump into a disenchanter and end up with a +5 saber...
which he then sat inside another vortex to re-enchant, and managed to
get it to +7.

Plane of Water was boring... basically sitting around in the bubble
killing sea monsters and WE's, until autosearch suddenly turned out
the portal close by. (He tried wearing the AoY; didn't help.)

Astral Plane was more interesting... he started out on the east wing,
and Famine somehow decided to come out from the north wing to meet
him, only to get distracted and wander off to the west where
Pestilence was. So the north wing was practically an open field for
Durak. Unfortunately, it wasn't the right altar. So then he had to
pass both Famine and Pestilence (didn't want to meet Death just yet).
Managed to dodge Famine, but came face-to-face with Pestilence. When
he realized that was inevitable, he quickly put on the =oConflict, and
sure enough, Pestilence fell after only one sickness attack, which was
cured with a !oHW. At this point Durak was at maximum carrying
capacity, and was hard pressed to take out any more !oHW. Good thing
Pestilence fell when he did. He worked his way to the west temple,
only to find that Pestilence had revived and was about to reach him
again, while a D was blocking Durak's way to the altar. The angels
behind the D kept zapping wands that killed off the insects that stood
between Durak and Pestilence... fortunately, he managed to escape JUST
before Pestilence reached him, and was able to maintain his distance
thereafter.

And then he found that the altar was the right one, and, indulging in
the final moments of mortality, he decided to kill off a pestering
arch lich while standing on the altar. And then he offered up the
Amulet, and brought along with him quite a large collection of
jewels (including *4* dilithium crystals!).


THE END


